{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/386118-going-off-purpose","id":386118,"title":"Going off purpose?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-30T03:57:24-08:00","id":386118,"title":"Going off purpose?","content":"It's mentioned in several places that mummies who shirk the purpose they were raised for burn out their Sekhem quicker than those who stay on task. However I can't find any mechanical rules for this. It would make sense if staying on purpose was factored into resets or provoked Descents somehow, or if shirking led to automatic success at Descent rolls (for a harsh ST), but I can't even find suggestions on how to incorporate this.<br /> <br /> Did I miss something, or does the community have suggested systems?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:19:41-08:00","id":386507,"title":"","content":"Descent rolls and Memory degradation are the twin lashes the Judges use to keep their favored pets in line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T12:21:39-08:00","id":386571,"title":"","content":"It's also important to remember that dealing with more immediate issues than a purpose that might take awhile to achieve is not necessarily going off-purpose. <br /> <br /> If you stay on purpose, sure, making a significant step towards that might provoke a Descent reset. <br /> <br /> I think it's intentionally left kind of narrative for the ST to do as they wish rather than trying to describe &quot;how far off-purpose you are&quot; in a table or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T14:52:06-08:00","id":386714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/386118-going-off-purpose?p=386507#post386507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Descent rolls and Memory degradation are the twin lashes the Judges use to keep their favored pets in line.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true, Descent rolls are the only ones the Judges can directly inflict. Memory only occurs when the descent ends, although each of the Judges encourages activities that <i>cause</i> Memory degradation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:11:07-08:00","id":388050,"title":"","content":"I agree that keeping &quot;how far off purpose&quot; in the hands of the storyteller is a good idea, but what I'm talking about is that there are no rules or guidelines for what to do once you've decided. My confusion is that despite several passages saying that mummies which ignore their purpose descend faster, the mechanics I can find offer no difference between the descent of a mummy who zealously obeys orders and that of one who runs as far away in the other direction as possible - or even actively counteracts their first purpose. So... what is an appropriate way of handling it (after the decision that they've gone off purpose has been determined)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-31T23:42:52-08:00","id":388087,"title":"","content":"Descent checks, obviously, the moment a Mummy has gone &quot;off purpose&quot; as decided by the GM. I would think it's pretty obviously intended to be resolved in the same way as any of the events listed on page 155 as warranting a Descent check. At the end of a scene in which a Mummy acted against their First Purpose, they cop a Descent check as punishment. That would cause them to descend faster than a Mummy who remains &quot;on purpose&quot;, especially if that Mummy were also seeking out opportunities for the Descent resets outlined on page 156.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}